From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: gen1: stop a closing decoder session at OUTPUT
 streamoff

With seek_mode=1, an OUTPUT streamoff that follows a CAPTURE streamoff
only flushes the session and keeps it loaded and started, so that the
next streamon continues it. iris_close() stops such a session before it
releases the m2m context.

When the file is released while both queues are still streaming, for
example because the process holding it died, v4l2_m2m_ctx_release()
streams both queues off itself, after that check. The OUTPUT streamoff
then takes the seek branch, SESSION_END goes to a session that is still
loaded and started, and the firmware rejects it, which puts the
instance in the error state. The driver then frees the internal buffers
while the firmware may still use them. Killing a raw V4L2 H.264 decode
mid-stream with SIGKILL left the session in the error state in 40 of 40
runs; 9 of them also hit an SMMU context fault on the video stream and
11 a firmware watchdog and reload. With seek_mode=0 none of 30 runs did,
and with this change none of 40.

A closing instance gets no further streamon, so stop it fully instead
of only flushing it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
index 48a0de6fa5..0e21b8eb92 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -236,13 +236,15 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen1_session_stop(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 				ret = iris_wait_for_session_response(inst, true);
 			}
 		} else if (READ_ONCE(iris_seek_mode) == 1 && V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane) &&
+			   !inst->closing &&
 			   inst->state == IRIS_INST_INPUT_STREAMING &&
 			   inst->sub_state & IRIS_INST_SUB_LOAD_RESOURCES) {
 			/*
 			 * OUTPUT streamoff after CAPTURE streamoff (a seek, or the first half of
 			 * a stop): flush and keep the session loaded and started, as venus
 			 * vdec_stop_output() does. The next streamon continues it;
-			 * iris_close() stops it if none comes.
+			 * iris_close() stops it if none comes. A closing instance
+			 * gets no further streamon, so it is stopped right here.
 			 */
 			reinit_completion(&inst->flush_completion);
 
